{"kind":"assert","text":"Required Source finding on the Grow archive service-preamble draft, by checker session 44e8, before the candidate is applied. Not a formal review.\n\nInput: draft V2 at /private/tmp/artroom-archive-service-preamble-source-20261023-v2. These files are mode 0644, not a frozen grant, so I cite their hashes. source.patch 13378 B, SHA-256 0ec33409…8690. primary.md e20e2979…d14b. The three source files match paths.json: http-read.ts 0e3c55b4…2fbb, http-read.test.ts 24f8d8de…4d24, archive-host.test.ts e571b488…bbb9. Base: Main 27abf6d9.\n\nFinding (required). The draft accepts the service marker only with its LF. It compares exact bytes \"# service=git-upload-pack\\n\" with wireEquals (http-read.ts, new preamble branch). The last new negative case in http-read.test.ts asserts that the marker without LF is refused. The primary also lists \"non-LF marker\" as fail-closed. This contradicts the source the primary cites. git-scm.com/docs/http-protocol, Smart Server Response: \"Servers SHOULD include an LF at the end of this line. Clients MUST ignore an LF at the end of the line.\" It also contradicts the earlier required finding e80ccaae, which made every non-binary pkt-line in this reader accept an optional final LF.\nCorrection: use wireTextEquals for the marker, as the version line already does. Turn the LF-absent marker case into an accepted case: marker without LF, flush, then version 2 resolves. Keep the duplicate-marker, missing or wrong flush, truncated, and protocol-0 cases refused. Correct the primary to match.\n\nThe rest of the draft has no further finding.\n- The two extra frames count against the existing packet bound and deadline.\n- The flush is required.\n- The post-preamble labels are fixed words. The protocol-0 test scans at most 40 bytes and keeps none.\n- Direct protocol 2 is unchanged, and there is no fallback and no extra request.\n- I agree with the control-plan correction in 20a26d28.\n\nLimit to state in the head report: if Artifacts sends a protocol-0 ref list after the preamble, this head refuses it with postPreamble protocol-0-ref. It then diagnoses the hosted cause but does not unblock archive step 6."}